"""Scoped existing evidence guide: original comparison worksheet, no new result claims."""
from pathlib import Path
import re
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];p=R/'guides/reading-str-case-study-results/index.html';s=p.read_text()
assert '"datePublished": "2026-10-04"' in s and '"dateModified": "2026-10-04"' in s
s=s.replace('"dateModified": "2026-10-04"','"dateModified": "2026-10-07"')
marker='        <h2>Apply the questions to your own deal</h2>'
assert s.count(marker)==1
body='''        <h2>Original two-file comparison before hiring a provider</h2>
        <p>A provider may show a forecast prepared before purchase and a later owner statement for the same house. Ask what each file establishes rather than treating the second as automatic confirmation of the first. Use this original comparison register for any company's example, including BNB Accelerator's. These requests are not a claim that private records have been authenticated or that every provider can disclose another client's documents.</p>
        <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Comparison field</th><th scope="col">Pre-purchase model</th><th scope="col">Operating record</th><th scope="col">Buyer question</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Period and availability</th><td>Intended annual window and assumed bookable nights</td><td>Actual covered months, opened date and owner-use or unavailable nights</td><td>Do these files describe the same opportunity to earn revenue?</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Income and cash timing</th><td>Forecast accommodation revenue and treatment of cleaning, taxes and refunds</td><td>Same-period booking exports, payouts and reconciliation</td><td>Are stay dates being mixed with payout dates or gross platform totals?</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Costs and financing</th><td>Fee bases, recurring costs, debt payments and reserve assumptions</td><td>Invoices and statements, actual debt payments and separately identified capital items</td><td>What expense was estimated, omitted or paid outside this statement?</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Capital and provenance</th><td>Planned total cash, model date and preparer</td><td>Actual funded cash, later additions, record source and review status</td><td>Can the numerator and denominator be reconciled without inventing missing amounts?</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
        <p><strong>Invented work sample only, not a client outcome:</strong> The pre-purchase model shows $20,000 annual owner cash flow on $160,000 planned cash invested, or 12.5%. A later record covers only six months and shows $36,000 accommodation revenue, $9,000 variable costs, $12,000 fixed costs and $10,000 debt payments. Those entries leave $5,000 before any omitted costs, capital spending or reserve contributions. Suppose final cash invested was $200,000 rather than the model's $160,000. That $5,000 is 2.5% of the stated capital for the covered six-month period, not an annual cash-on-cash return or a complete verified return.</p>
        <p>Do not double the six-month figure into a $10,000 annual forecast: the unobserved months may have different demand, availability and costs. Do not describe the difference from the original 12.5% as a measured full-year loss of performance; both period and denominator changed. First obtain the missing months and reconcile exclusions. If the documents cannot support that comparison, keep it unresolved and underwrite your candidate independently. No hypothetical file here establishes service quality, misconduct, typical performance or what your purchase will earn.</p>
        <h2>Turn an unresolved result into a purchase question</h2>
        <p>Ask for the definition, covered period, reconciled totals and consented supporting evidence, not another customer's passwords, tax return or unrestricted booking file. Redacted or aggregated records may support a limited purpose; record what remains unverified. A confidentiality limit is not proof a claim is false, and a polished screenshot is not independent verification. Keep seller and client material in a secure private deal file; do not publish it as proof without permission.</p>
        <p>If the cash denominator differs, obtain the full acquisition-and-launch schedule. If expenses are missing, run your own model with actual quotes. If a success story uses only selected high-performing months, ask about the rest of the period without assuming the result is typical or atypical. Before paying a service fee, use the <a href="/blog/str-buyer-agent-vs-acquisition-team/">one-property provider work-sample test</a> to see how the team handles your own unresolved questions. The <a href="/compare/">comparison hub</a> separates named service paths; a testimonial alone does not choose the right contracted scope.</p>
        <p>Evidence worksheet reviewed October 7, 2026. BNB Accelerator is the commercially interested publisher and acquisition provider. This is an original document-review method and labeled hypothetical arithmetic, not firsthand provider testing, independent auditing or an authenticated customer-results study. Your own advisers must assess the proposed property and actual agreements.</p>

'''
s=s.replace(marker,body+marker);p.write_text(s)
p=R/'sitemap-core.xml';s=p.read_text();s,n=re.subn(r'(<loc>https://www\.bnbaccelerator\.com/guides/reading-str-case-study-results/</loc>\s*<lastmod>)2026-10-04',r'\g<1>2026-10-07',s);assert n==1;p.write_text(s)
